**Primal formulation:** For each window `W=[l,r]` (length m), with `kk = min(k, m, n-m)`:
- `gain(W) = max over t≤kk of (sum of t largest outside) - (sum of t smallest inside)`
- Since swap gains are nonincreasing: if `b₀ ≥ a₀` (kk-th largest outside ≥ kk-th smallest inside), `gain = B_kk - A_kk` (do all kk swaps); else `gain = min_v [In(v) + Out(v)]` where the optimal threshold `v* =` the **(n-m)-th smallest element of the whole array** (provable via slope analysis), and `In(v)=Σ_in(v-x)⁺`, `Out(v)=Σ_out(x-v)⁺`.

**Fast incremental maintenance:** For fixed `l`, extend `r`, keeping inside/outside in sorted lists (bisect + C-speed insert/delete). The sums `A_kk`, `B_kk` update in O(1) per insert/delete/kk-change, thresholds `a₀`,`b₀` read in O(1), and `In/Out` maintain in amortized O(1) since `v*` is monotone in m. Let me implement and verify against brute force:
